1
00:00:06,710 --> 00:02:10,870
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:13,730
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the compassionate, the merciful)

3
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:23,250
Now that they have captured Osman...

4
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:24,800
they want information.

5
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:28,310
They think that they'll have the treasure.

6
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,410
Sir...

7
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:31,450
What's your command?

8
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:33,790
You'll go to the castle as the ambassador.

9
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:35,820
Tell them...

10
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:39,400
Edebalı will give you the treasure.

11
00:02:41,130 --> 00:02:42,440
But...

12
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:47,150
if they let Osman out.

13
00:02:47,550 --> 00:02:49,080
Sir...

14
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:52,100
We have struggled for years to have them.

15
00:02:53,070 --> 00:02:55,370
Lots of our friends died.

16
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,530
Is it worth for Osman?

17
00:02:57,580 --> 00:03:02,820
We took back the dignity of the World of
Islam from them, Akçaderviş.

18
00:03:03,150 --> 00:03:07,150
But Osman is as valuable as the treasure.

19
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:10,840
But will we really give
them the treasure, sir?

20
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:13,750
If we take Osman, then yes.

21
00:03:15,090 --> 00:03:17,550
I'll be waiting for Yannis.

22
00:03:18,310 --> 00:03:20,560
Let us go with you, father.

23
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:24,370
Go to Kayı Tent, Bala.

24
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:28,400
If anything crucial happens
there, let us know.

25
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:31,410
The devil is also there.

26
00:03:31,650 --> 00:03:35,480
Take care of it if necessary.

27
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:39,320
Your command, father. Where are you going?

28
00:03:39,710 --> 00:03:43,630
Ashes to ashes, dust to dust.

29
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:49,070
May our holy war be blessed.

30
00:04:14,690 --> 00:04:16,330
Hit me! So...

31
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:20,490
life will squirt instead of blood!

32
00:04:21,130 --> 00:04:22,870
Hope will squirt!

33
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:25,490
Hit me!

34
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:26,720
Hit!

35
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:30,010
Talk! Where is Edebalı?

36
00:04:34,970 --> 00:04:37,800
Talk! Or I'll kill you...

37
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:40,970
and your men. (Alps)

38
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:46,520
Talk!

39
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:47,700
Where?!

40
00:04:47,890 --> 00:04:48,990
Talk!

41
00:04:50,850 --> 00:04:52,310
Come closer...

42
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:00,110
Come closer.

43
00:05:12,010 --> 00:05:16,010
He's in our hearts.

44
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:20,000
In my heart.

45
00:05:20,230 --> 00:05:23,590
In all of Turk's hearts including me.

46
00:05:24,870 --> 00:05:28,190
If you are strong enough...

47
00:05:28,450 --> 00:05:30,770
take him!

48
00:06:04,570 --> 00:06:06,690
Devil! Come!

49
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:09,640
- Boğaç.
- Come!

50
00:06:14,770 --> 00:06:15,990
No.

51
00:06:19,490 --> 00:06:21,490
- Boğaç!
- Brother.

52
00:06:21,490 --> 00:06:22,950
Boğaç!

53
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:26,450
Brother!

54
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:32,370
My Bey...

55
00:06:51,150 --> 00:06:52,360
Boğaç...

56
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:05,200
I hear a weak groaning, Osman.

57
00:07:05,990 --> 00:07:09,990
- Do you hear it too?
- Lions roar, Sofia.

58
00:07:10,030 --> 00:07:11,110
They don't groan.

59
00:07:11,110 --> 00:07:16,790
Our dungeons are full of bones
of lions, Osman.

60
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:21,710
Hold on, brother. Hold on.

61
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:27,310
Allah is eternal!

62
00:07:27,690 --> 00:07:29,290
Boğaç!

63
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:38,720
Allah says in Al-Baqarah...

64
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:43,580
"Or do you think that you
will enter Heaven...

65
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:47,990
while such [trial] has not yet come
to you as came to those...

66
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:53,210
who passed on before you?" [2:214]

67
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:02,220
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

68
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:06,100
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

69
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:09,210
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

70
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:12,410
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

71
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:14,900
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

72
00:08:15,050 --> 00:08:19,900
- Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)
- Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

73
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:24,000
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

74
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:29,180
- Shut up!
- Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

75
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:35,730
- Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)
- Shut these dogs up!

76
00:08:35,950 --> 00:08:40,560
- Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)
- Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

77
00:08:41,450 --> 00:08:46,010
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

78
00:08:46,930 --> 00:08:51,510
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

79
00:08:53,150 --> 00:08:57,150
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

80
00:08:58,590 --> 00:09:02,590
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

81
00:09:11,710 --> 00:09:16,620
Here! It's the picture of my victory!

82
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:44,140
Dündar Bey, I know who has done it.

83
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:45,850
Tell us what to do.

84
00:09:45,870 --> 00:09:49,700
Kayı's horses will make Kulucahisar Castle
unbearable to unbelievers.

85
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:52,730
What does it have to do with Kulucahisar?

86
00:09:52,890 --> 00:09:56,150
Sofia and Kalanoz came to our tent.

87
00:09:56,250 --> 00:09:58,220
They want friendship.

88
00:09:58,230 --> 00:10:01,840
We don't know who has done this.

89
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:05,560
Süleyman Shah's tent!

90
00:10:05,580 --> 00:10:09,230
What is that? Your tent...

91
00:10:09,230 --> 00:10:12,300
don't know the difference
between friend and foe!

92
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:17,540
I saw that devil's treachery!

93
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:20,930
How can you not see her real face?

94
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:25,800
This tent isn't like where you come from,
Selcan Hatun.

95
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:28,850
This tent is sensitive...

96
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:31,870
and it has deep politics.

97
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:34,970
If you hadn't run away
from your husband...

98
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:38,340
you would've known it.

99
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:42,630
Your mind is poor, your mouth is pedant.

100
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:48,600
You try to teach us politics without
looking at yourself.

101
00:10:48,910 --> 00:10:52,690
Your time is up, Selcan Hatun.

102
00:10:54,230 --> 00:10:59,650
If you try to barge in, I won't be just
pedant, you should know.

103
00:11:00,350 --> 00:11:02,530
Look at this panache, Bamsı.

104
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:05,080
She thinks that she's a Sultan.

105
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:08,310
Don't make me angry.

106
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:11,590
- Pull yourself together, Zöhre!
- Shut up!

107
00:11:11,630 --> 00:11:13,540
Selcan Hatun.

108
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:17,360
Selcan Hatun...

109
00:11:19,130 --> 00:11:21,910
Selcan Hatun.

110
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:28,580
If you dare to talk that way
again in front of me...

111
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:31,900
I'll cut your tongues.

112
00:11:36,860 --> 00:11:42,850
Now, leave the field of
contest to us, men.

113
00:11:43,510 --> 00:11:46,600
Mind your own businesses. Hatuns!

114
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:48,250
Out!

115
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:53,420
- Dündar Bey...
- I said out!

116
00:12:00,230 --> 00:12:02,100
Dündar Bey...

117
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:05,920
It's obvious that Kayı's
torment is forgotten.

118
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:08,120
Bring them into line as soon as possible.

119
00:12:15,450 --> 00:12:19,450
Osman is my son.

120
00:12:21,130 --> 00:12:24,420
We can't sleep or rest...

121
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:26,700
till we find him.

122
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:31,200
But something big is going on.

123
00:12:32,450 --> 00:12:36,080
To rescue Osman...

124
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:40,690
we'll lie in ambush like a
wolf, roar like a lion...

125
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:45,440
and we'll be cunning.

126
00:12:53,030 --> 00:12:57,030
Now, listen to me carefully.

127
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:03,670
Big devil...

128
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:06,410
Welcome.

129
00:13:09,550 --> 00:13:11,810
You'll all die.

130
00:13:12,740 --> 00:13:17,880
Our biggest pleasure is to
persecute you, Osman.

131
00:13:18,300 --> 00:13:20,600
Pain is fine.

132
00:13:21,270 --> 00:13:23,250
Suffering is fine.

133
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:26,690
Don't get nervous, Osman. We have time.

134
00:13:28,270 --> 00:13:32,810
We'll listen to your sayings, Osman.

135
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:39,590
Princess Sofia. Well done.

136
00:13:40,050 --> 00:13:42,750
Turks will do some things.

137
00:13:42,770 --> 00:13:46,540
They'll look for Osman in the castle.

138
00:13:46,910 --> 00:13:50,290
They shall keep
thinking that you're an angel.

139
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:54,710
Don't worry, sir.

140
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:03,010
Good luck, Osman.

141
00:14:26,020 --> 00:14:28,000
Gündüz Bey...

142
00:14:28,050 --> 00:14:30,200
We can't underestimate things that are
said.

143
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:35,960
Go to the castle with
Bamsı Bey and meet Sofia.

144
00:14:37,940 --> 00:14:41,940
Make them feel my anger.

145
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:46,110
Tell them...

146
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:51,980
If our friends involve in preparing
Osman's trap...

147
00:14:53,010 --> 00:14:58,330
we'll kill them one by one.

148
00:14:59,730 --> 00:15:01,570
Your command, my Bey.

149
00:15:02,930 --> 00:15:04,830
Thanks, Dündar Bey.

150
00:15:05,220 --> 00:15:08,580
I have some business with that centipede.

151
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:12,500
You're going there for Osman, Bamsı Bey.

152
00:15:12,890 --> 00:15:14,570
Don't forget it.

153
00:15:15,690 --> 00:15:19,690
And we won't have unfinished businesses.

154
00:15:21,230 --> 00:15:22,330
Batur...

155
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:27,050
You must send your Alps (men)
to everywhere.

156
00:15:28,490 --> 00:15:32,130
Your eyes are strong, your
ears are strong.

157
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:36,110
They'll search everywhere.

158
00:15:36,230 --> 00:15:39,290
If they find a trace...

159
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:41,540
let us know.

160
00:15:41,830 --> 00:15:43,780
Your command.

161
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:49,420
I thought you were cleverer.

162
00:15:49,550 --> 00:15:53,550
You fell prey to me in
your first struggle.

163
00:15:53,650 --> 00:15:56,400
It's too early to celebrate your victory.

164
00:15:57,070 --> 00:15:59,570
We just began.

165
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:01,970
Thank Allah that...

166
00:16:02,530 --> 00:16:05,840
I have an enemy like you.

167
00:16:10,820 --> 00:16:14,820
Did you learn these
words from your father?

168
00:16:15,890 --> 00:16:19,780
You want to know where
Sheikh Edebalı is, right?

169
00:16:20,710 --> 00:16:25,130
You want to find where the treasures are.

170
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:30,140
Actually, I don't care about your
treasures.

171
00:16:33,270 --> 00:16:37,270
I just want to destroy your dignity.

172
00:16:38,670 --> 00:16:42,220
If you take possession of
a nation's belongings...

173
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:45,840
you take their honor.

174
00:16:46,690 --> 00:16:51,350
I already have so many of these treasures.

175
00:16:54,490 --> 00:16:56,960
You may take our treasure...

176
00:16:57,460 --> 00:16:58,390
but...

177
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:01,670
not our soul.

178
00:17:03,070 --> 00:17:07,200
Happiness goes, traditions
stay, says our ancestors.

179
00:17:08,090 --> 00:17:13,990
We rivet our traditions to our
hearts and minds.

180
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:17,930
Even if there's only one
Turk left in the world...

181
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:20,990
it means that our traditions are alive!

182
00:17:22,140 --> 00:17:25,130
And that one Turk's aim...

183
00:17:25,410 --> 00:17:28,490
to wreck your rule!

184
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:53,770
Here, Osman Bey.

185
00:17:54,060 --> 00:17:55,840
You must be thirsty.

186
00:18:28,990 --> 00:18:32,990
You're so angry, Osman!

187
00:18:39,990 --> 00:18:41,370
Is it ready?

188
00:19:01,530 --> 00:19:03,730
Ah, fire!

189
00:19:04,210 --> 00:19:09,470
Fire that melts the mountains!

190
00:19:15,210 --> 00:19:18,120
Show us your strength!

191
00:19:44,130 --> 00:19:46,770
- Degenerated!
- Devil!

192
00:19:46,910 --> 00:19:49,990
You have nice friends, Osman!

193
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:54,800
When you're hurt, they yell!

194
00:19:57,280 --> 00:20:00,370
Is that all you can, Yannis?

195
00:20:14,460 --> 00:20:18,110
Witness my victory, Osman.

196
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:21,390
Megela.

197
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:32,680
Where is Edebalı?

198
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:52,130
Where is Edebalı?!

199
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:04,270
In the name of Allah, the
compassionate, the merciful.

200
00:21:04,750 --> 00:21:07,790
"Indeed, We have given you, (Muhammad),
a clear conquest...

201
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:14,310
"That Allah may forgive for you what preceded of your sin and what will follow and...

202
00:21:14,860 --> 00:21:18,070
complete His favor upon you...

203
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:23,170
...and
guide you to a straight path."

204
00:21:30,860 --> 00:21:35,000
"And Allah may aid you
with a mighty victory."

205
00:21:37,210 --> 00:21:41,210
"It is He who sent down tranquillity into
the hearts of the believers...

206
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:45,230
...that they would increase in faith along
with their [present] faith."

207
00:21:45,770 --> 00:21:49,060
"And to Allah belong the soldiers of the heavens and the earth...

208
00:21:49,230 --> 00:21:52,280
...and ever is Allah Knowing...

209
00:21:52,690 --> 00:21:55,860
... and Wise." Surah Al-Fath [48]

210
00:21:59,050 --> 00:22:01,010
Allah.

211
00:22:02,380 --> 00:22:04,550
Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest.)

212
00:22:05,660 --> 00:22:08,320
Enough!

213
00:22:10,730 --> 00:22:12,580
Enough.

214
00:22:16,650 --> 00:22:19,590
I'll tell where Edebalı is.

215
00:22:21,630 --> 00:22:24,440
I'm listening, Osman.

216
00:22:24,530 --> 00:22:26,920
Where is Edebalı?

217
00:22:33,010 --> 00:22:35,450
Master Yannis! Master Yannis!

218
00:22:35,530 --> 00:22:39,340
- Allah is eternal!
- Allah is eternal!

219
00:22:39,460 --> 00:22:43,290
- Allah is eternal!
- You dogs!

220
00:22:49,370 --> 00:22:51,440
Sir...

221
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:59,180
Master Yannis! Master Yannis!

222
00:23:38,130 --> 00:23:40,070
Any news from Osman Bey, Batur?

223
00:23:40,070 --> 00:23:43,770
Aren't you his servant? You
couldn't save your Bey.

224
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:47,440
We've brought enemies to their knees...

225
00:23:48,740 --> 00:23:51,290
but we also have enemies inside.

226
00:23:51,760 --> 00:23:54,870
Inshaallah, you don't betray us.

227
00:23:55,710 --> 00:23:58,460
Or I'll kill you.

228
00:23:58,660 --> 00:24:03,410
You couldn't save your Bey but
you keep showing off here.

229
00:24:03,900 --> 00:24:05,410
If you were that brave...

230
00:24:05,450 --> 00:24:09,650
what were you doing when
Osman was abducted?

231
00:24:13,290 --> 00:24:15,880
You're evil, Batur.

232
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:18,200
But I promised Bamsı Bey.

233
00:24:18,460 --> 00:24:22,460
I won't be like devil till we
make the enemies kneel down.

234
00:24:23,230 --> 00:24:25,400
If I hear
one more treachery...

235
00:24:25,410 --> 00:24:29,230
no one can save you from me!

236
00:24:30,740 --> 00:24:32,940
That's enough, Samsa.

237
00:24:33,210 --> 00:24:38,180
Go to Kayı Tent and obey my father
Dündar Bey now.

238
00:24:40,730 --> 00:24:44,110
Our Ertuğrul Bey gave the
power to my father.

239
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:07,140
My Allah, you're the greatest.

240
00:25:07,690 --> 00:25:09,900
My Allah, you're the greatest.

241
00:25:21,830 --> 00:25:24,370
What is this visit for?

242
00:25:25,200 --> 00:25:27,420
That's not a visit, Sofia.

243
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:30,610
We're here to call out.

244
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:33,730
An attack, maybe a betrayal.

245
00:25:34,410 --> 00:25:36,570
You'll tell us which.

246
00:25:36,930 --> 00:25:39,420
I don't know what you're talking about.

247
00:25:42,090 --> 00:25:44,730
What attack? What betrayal?

248
00:25:45,070 --> 00:25:47,840
Osman Bey and his Alps (men)
have been attacked.

249
00:25:48,020 --> 00:25:49,700
No need to talk more.

250
00:25:49,700 --> 00:25:53,460
If this has anything to do
with Kulucahisar...

251
00:25:53,500 --> 00:25:55,310
you should be frightened.

252
00:25:55,360 --> 00:26:01,130
You're threatening us in our lands,
in our castle, Gündüz Bey.

253
00:26:01,220 --> 00:26:03,610
We don't, Kalanoz!

254
00:26:08,820 --> 00:26:11,480
It's a command of Dündar Bey, son
of Süleyman Shah.

255
00:26:12,210 --> 00:26:15,280
If you are the people who
killed our Alps and...

256
00:26:16,030 --> 00:26:20,030
intended to kill our Beys ...

257
00:26:20,620 --> 00:26:23,470
Kayı's wrath will be on you.

258
00:26:23,500 --> 00:26:28,590
I swear to Allah...

259
00:26:29,450 --> 00:26:33,310
we'll come to your door with our horses.

260
00:26:34,310 --> 00:26:37,860
We'll break your door with punches...

261
00:26:41,750 --> 00:26:44,930
and we'll make your
tombstones with it.

262
00:26:46,260 --> 00:26:48,780
I swear to Allah, we will Sofia.

263
00:26:49,470 --> 00:26:51,750
We will.

264
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:06,020
I know you're in pain, Bamsı Bey.

265
00:27:09,690 --> 00:27:12,940
We're your most powerful ally.

266
00:27:14,050 --> 00:27:16,160
Why do we do something like this?

267
00:27:16,800 --> 00:27:20,260
We killed traitor Yannis.

268
00:27:21,050 --> 00:27:23,200
Just to strengthen our friendship.

269
00:27:28,970 --> 00:27:32,060
I lost my husband for this deal.

270
00:27:33,030 --> 00:27:37,030
If anyone prevents this deal to happen...

271
00:27:38,170 --> 00:27:40,780
I'll kill him!

272
00:27:45,140 --> 00:27:46,680
Commander Kalanoz!

273
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:53,040
It's my order to all soldiers
in Kulucahisar Castle.

274
00:27:54,100 --> 00:27:59,020
Osman Bey, our powerful ally who
is the Bey of Kayı Tent...

275
00:27:59,020 --> 00:28:01,460
will be searched everywhere.

276
00:28:01,740 --> 00:28:05,460
Everything that hurt
him will be destroyed.

277
00:28:05,500 --> 00:28:09,500
Until we hear from him, we won't stop.

278
00:28:09,500 --> 00:28:11,270
Your command.

279
00:28:15,710 --> 00:28:19,730
Stop feeling suspicious
about us, Gündüz Bey.

280
00:28:20,120 --> 00:28:24,520
As long as there is peace, we'll all win.

281
00:28:24,610 --> 00:28:26,450
Thanks.

282
00:28:26,700 --> 00:28:29,680
Princess Sofia, thanks.

283
00:28:31,570 --> 00:28:33,020
Sofia...

284
00:28:34,340 --> 00:28:38,630
These eyes, these eyes...

285
00:28:40,950 --> 00:28:45,610
saw so many cunnings looking like a sheep.

286
00:28:47,570 --> 00:28:53,170
At the end, these cunnings' peltries
became my shoes.

287
00:28:57,990 --> 00:29:00,870
You should know that.

288
00:29:04,580 --> 00:29:06,320
Come on, my Gündüz.

289
00:29:07,700 --> 00:29:10,380
Let's go.

290
00:29:12,030 --> 00:29:14,230
Thanks, Bamsı Bey.

291
00:29:36,540 --> 00:29:38,780
Sir, are you okay?

292
00:30:12,370 --> 00:30:14,470
He's powerful.

293
00:30:15,720 --> 00:30:18,080
Like a tiger.

294
00:30:19,690 --> 00:30:22,130
He won't talk.

295
00:30:23,110 --> 00:30:27,110
When he's sober, continue torturing him.

296
00:30:27,440 --> 00:30:29,880
- Where are you going, sir?
- To the castle.

297
00:30:30,430 --> 00:30:33,540
Edebalı will reach me for Osman.

298
00:30:33,860 --> 00:30:37,160
Your men should be careful.

299
00:30:37,350 --> 00:30:39,240
Your command, sir.

300
00:30:39,770 --> 00:30:44,660
Kayıs smell the blood quickly.

301
00:31:12,800 --> 00:31:15,670
He is Marcus!

302
00:31:21,330 --> 00:31:22,870
Yes, it's him!

303
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:29,440
Why are you here, traitor? Traitor!
What are you doing here?

304
00:31:30,270 --> 00:31:32,020
Priest Marcus!

305
00:31:34,080 --> 00:31:37,230
Traitor! What are you doing here?

306
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:40,140
Kill him! Kill him!

307
00:31:46,910 --> 00:31:48,840
Tursun!

308
00:31:49,110 --> 00:31:51,350
Soldiers! Take him!

309
00:32:13,330 --> 00:32:16,400
If anyone interferes, he'll be dead.

310
00:32:17,640 --> 00:32:19,700
You'll take me to Sofia.

311
00:32:20,680 --> 00:32:22,930
Edebalı sends his regards.

312
00:32:39,020 --> 00:32:41,640
Eat it. Eat.

313
00:32:45,080 --> 00:32:47,740
Easy, easy!

314
00:32:47,970 --> 00:32:50,590
Don't die. I need you.

315
00:33:06,480 --> 00:33:08,540
Why are you doing this?

316
00:33:09,820 --> 00:33:11,730
What do you want from me?

317
00:33:12,010 --> 00:33:14,520
Even if we're on different sides...

318
00:33:14,990 --> 00:33:16,800
we have the same enemy.

319
00:33:18,470 --> 00:33:19,840
Osman.

320
00:33:34,100 --> 00:33:35,870
Listen to me carefully.

321
00:33:37,130 --> 00:33:41,770
Osman is trouble when
both alive and dead.

322
00:33:46,980 --> 00:33:49,570
Tell me where he is.

323
00:33:54,130 --> 00:33:56,370
I have to protect the
dignity of my father.

324
00:34:02,360 --> 00:34:04,580
I don't care about your father's dignity.

325
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:07,910
I can't tell you where he is.

326
00:34:10,700 --> 00:34:12,590
I want him...

327
00:34:13,300 --> 00:34:15,220
dead...

328
00:34:18,420 --> 00:34:20,020
not alive.

329
00:34:25,300 --> 00:34:29,300
Osman is an obstacle.

330
00:34:30,890 --> 00:34:33,820
We go hunting, he is the head hunter.

331
00:34:33,910 --> 00:34:36,140
We organize something, he
is the head of it.

332
00:34:36,270 --> 00:34:40,110
Osman is always the most powerful!

333
00:34:40,240 --> 00:34:43,530
And I'm always the one who is in the back.

334
00:34:44,680 --> 00:34:48,000
If I don't kill him, I'll always
be in the back.

335
00:34:51,870 --> 00:34:54,130
I'll kill you...

336
00:34:54,530 --> 00:34:58,900
or I'll give you double the money
you have in your lap.

337
00:35:00,080 --> 00:35:04,080
There is not much to think of. You want
Osman's head from me.

338
00:35:04,670 --> 00:35:08,450
Just tell me about the gold.
I'd even kill my father.

339
00:35:13,040 --> 00:35:18,470
I'll be waiting at the riverside.
Bring me Osman's head by the night.

340
00:35:19,570 --> 00:35:23,570
But, no gold until I see his head.
Know that.

341
00:35:34,150 --> 00:35:36,280
That was a good agreement.

342
00:35:39,510 --> 00:35:42,230
That was a good agreement.

343
00:36:28,870 --> 00:36:31,170
Is anyone here?

344
00:36:34,140 --> 00:36:36,270
Is anyone here?

345
00:36:40,100 --> 00:36:42,080
Is anyone here?

346
00:36:42,370 --> 00:36:44,770
Well, you're here, son.

347
00:36:44,930 --> 00:36:46,060
Edebali!

348
00:36:46,170 --> 00:36:48,370
Who else do you need?

349
00:36:50,240 --> 00:36:51,930
Edebali!

350
00:36:53,090 --> 00:36:54,910
Where are you?

351
00:36:54,910 --> 00:36:58,960
The creatures called humans, keep their
loved ones in their hearts, son.

352
00:36:59,550 --> 00:37:02,320
Don't look for me anywhere else.

353
00:37:09,080 --> 00:37:13,150
Thank heavens! Thank heavens!

354
00:37:14,720 --> 00:37:16,750
Edebali!

355
00:37:19,120 --> 00:37:23,210
They tied my hands and arms. I'm helpless!

356
00:37:26,260 --> 00:37:29,390
I have no more strength.

357
00:37:37,470 --> 00:37:44,910
Find real freedom in serving Allah, and
you shall never be captured, son.

358
00:37:45,400 --> 00:37:47,860
What is all this pain for?

359
00:37:49,830 --> 00:37:52,360
How do I get out of this?

360
00:37:53,440 --> 00:37:57,440
The solution is within the trouble.

361
00:37:58,200 --> 00:38:00,250
You'll see.

362
00:38:12,350 --> 00:38:14,600
Take this, son.

363
00:38:18,670 --> 00:38:20,640
Take it.

364
00:38:35,420 --> 00:38:37,410
Take it.

365
00:38:39,360 --> 00:38:40,980
Take it.

366
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:24,590
Separate the clay from the mud.

367
00:39:24,590 --> 00:39:28,210
Separate it, so that you learn it.

368
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:32,800
Learn it, so that you get wiser.

369
00:39:34,140 --> 00:39:38,500
The real treasure is knowledge,
little Osman.

370
00:39:38,570 --> 00:39:44,540
Treasures are only apparent to those
who know how to see them.

371
00:39:45,140 --> 00:39:51,690
Did you think Allah who sees, hears,
knows everything...

372
00:39:51,690 --> 00:39:54,450
... has forgotten about you?

373
00:39:55,500 --> 00:39:59,610
Do you think his servant came
and tied you up?

374
00:40:01,690 --> 00:40:05,420
Clear yourself of your doubts, son.

375
00:40:06,040 --> 00:40:09,790
Separate the clay, and reach the treasure.

376
00:40:13,040 --> 00:40:18,250
"For indeed, with hardship [will be] ease."
Surah Ash-Sharh (The Relief) [94:5]

377
00:40:19,340 --> 00:40:24,340
"For indeed, with hardship [will be] ease."
Surah Ash-Sharh (The Relief) [94:5]

378
00:40:24,980 --> 00:40:31,390
"For indeed, with hardship [will be] ease."

379
00:40:47,280 --> 00:40:55,530
"For indeed, with hardship [will be] ease."

380
00:40:58,170 --> 00:41:03,380
"For indeed, with hardship [will be] ease."

381
00:41:12,710 --> 00:41:17,820
"For indeed, with hardship [will be] ease."

382
00:41:22,640 --> 00:41:27,560
"For indeed, with hardship [will be] ease."

383
00:41:28,410 --> 00:41:32,410
"For indeed, with hardship [will be] ease."

384
00:41:34,610 --> 00:41:39,250
"For indeed, with hardship [will be] ease."

385
00:41:41,380 --> 00:41:46,610
"For indeed, with hardship [will be] ease."

386
00:41:50,900 --> 00:41:55,860
"For indeed, with hardship [will be] ease.

387
00:42:28,470 --> 00:42:30,240
Bala Hatun.

388
00:42:35,040 --> 00:42:40,850
Easy there. Your speed is racing
your shamelessness.

389
00:42:41,610 --> 00:42:44,660
We kick you out from the door,
you enter from the chimney.

390
00:42:44,660 --> 00:42:46,910
Aren't you ashamed?

391
00:42:46,910 --> 00:42:50,000
You don't know morals, just like how
you don't know your place.

392
00:42:50,490 --> 00:42:54,000
Since when it is in the Turkish law
to kick the guests out?

393
00:42:54,000 --> 00:42:59,050
I know what to say, but you don't
know where to stand.

394
00:43:00,100 --> 00:43:04,910
You came here and caused a lot of trouble.

395
00:43:04,910 --> 00:43:08,100
Osman will die because of you!

396
00:43:08,100 --> 00:43:12,270
How much more blood do you want to
be spilled? Isn't it enough?

397
00:43:12,270 --> 00:43:16,160
Do you cry like this in every
slight inconvenience?

398
00:43:16,160 --> 00:43:19,280
As if you grew up in a palace, and
not in the tent.

399
00:43:19,610 --> 00:43:25,150
Aygül sister, if you have big dreams,
keep your heart ready for it.

400
00:43:26,110 --> 00:43:29,080
So it doesn't get crushed during
every struggle.

401
00:43:33,250 --> 00:43:37,360
If you raise those hands to me again,
I'll poke your eyes out.

402
00:43:39,280 --> 00:43:41,350
Hatuns!

403
00:43:44,160 --> 00:43:46,070
Aygül!

404
00:43:49,600 --> 00:43:52,200
What is going on in the middle of
the Tent?

405
00:43:52,210 --> 00:43:57,370
Troubles are raining on us, aunt Selcan!
Because of them!

406
00:43:58,480 --> 00:44:02,480
And now they are back on our door like
they have no shame!

407
00:44:03,750 --> 00:44:07,590
Bala, go to the pavilion.

408
00:44:16,110 --> 00:44:19,240
Mind your own business now. Come on!

409
00:44:22,060 --> 00:44:26,490
Aygül, seems like you're forgetting.
Let me remind you.

410
00:44:26,910 --> 00:44:31,320
You're the daughter of a Bey.
Your biggest ornament is your politeness.

411
00:44:31,320 --> 00:44:32,990
That's the first thing.

412
00:44:32,990 --> 00:44:37,420
Osman risked his life for Bala Hatun.

413
00:44:37,420 --> 00:44:43,040
From now on, no one can separate them,
including you. That's the second thing.

414
00:44:45,110 --> 00:44:48,230
Remember these words.

415
00:44:49,910 --> 00:44:54,130
Don't push my patience too much.
That's the third thing.

416
00:45:15,720 --> 00:45:18,530
What is this, Andreas?

417
00:45:19,510 --> 00:45:23,460
What do you think you're doing
appearing before me with a simple priest?

418
00:45:24,500 --> 00:45:30,170
Relax, Sofia.
Your old friend has come to visit you.

419
00:45:30,850 --> 00:45:33,310
- What's there to get angry about?
- Soldiers!

420
00:45:33,310 --> 00:45:36,710
Take another step and Andreas dies!

421
00:45:43,530 --> 00:45:46,200
I brought Edebali's offer.

422
00:45:48,990 --> 00:45:54,280
Master Yannis was right
again, Priest Marcus.

423
00:45:54,280 --> 00:45:56,940
You came on your own.

424
00:45:58,480 --> 00:46:01,600
You'll bring the treasure too.

425
00:46:08,570 --> 00:46:10,720
I'm listening.

426
00:46:10,720 --> 00:46:16,430
Not a single word until Yannis comes.

427
00:46:18,920 --> 00:46:23,420
I'll wait for him here.
I hope I don't disturb you much.

428
00:46:30,110 --> 00:46:34,010
- Is there anything new from Osman Bey?
- No.

429
00:46:34,510 --> 00:46:39,520
Nothing new. But I know all of this is
that redhead's doings.

430
00:46:40,490 --> 00:46:44,180
Kulucahisar's devils are playing with us.

431
00:46:46,920 --> 00:46:50,180
They don't know what really
matters is destiny.

432
00:46:51,440 --> 00:46:54,660
Only if I could demolish that
castle of theirs!

433
00:46:55,070 --> 00:46:59,070
Let Osman Bey come back first, then it
will be their turn.

434
00:47:00,050 --> 00:47:04,300
Allah knows what will happen to my Osman.

435
00:47:06,400 --> 00:47:10,720
Osman is our Tents prosperity.
May Allah protect him.

436
00:47:15,140 --> 00:47:19,090
My father sent me here after hearing
about Osman Bey.

437
00:47:19,090 --> 00:47:23,010
He wants to give you a helping hand.

438
00:47:24,180 --> 00:47:27,040
May Allah bless you.

439
00:47:50,810 --> 00:47:53,590
Looks like you get along pretty well.

440
00:47:54,520 --> 00:47:57,940
Don't people listen to Beys in
this Tent anymore?

441
00:48:00,300 --> 00:48:04,300
Are unwelcome ones highly respected now?

442
00:48:19,120 --> 00:48:23,120
!ARABIC!

443
00:48:38,610 --> 00:48:42,610
!ARABIC!

444
00:48:49,910 --> 00:48:54,100
!ARABIC!

445
00:49:14,410 --> 00:49:18,540
Thank you, my Allah. Thank you.

446
00:49:19,270 --> 00:49:23,270
My Allah! My Allah!

447
00:49:28,600 --> 00:49:31,470
My Bey!

448
00:50:20,670 --> 00:50:24,050
A lion who passes out after being beaten.

449
00:50:30,130 --> 00:50:32,810
You should see it's claws too.

450
00:50:40,640 --> 00:50:43,340
Allah is eternal!

451
00:50:47,040 --> 00:50:49,700
Allah almighty!

452
00:50:55,600 --> 00:51:00,220
Did you lose yourself, now
that your Dündar Bey is a deputy?

453
00:51:00,220 --> 00:51:05,380
If my Bey is a deputy, then I'm
Kayı Tent's Hatun.

454
00:51:09,450 --> 00:51:14,450
If someone does wrong, I'll level them.

455
00:51:15,500 --> 00:51:18,280
No one else is needed.

456
00:51:18,280 --> 00:51:22,470
Good. You'll start with your
daughter then.

457
00:51:23,050 --> 00:51:25,030
Tent's Hatun...

458
00:51:32,860 --> 00:51:36,860
Dündar Bey neither wants Edebali, nor
his daughter in this Tent.

459
00:51:39,500 --> 00:51:43,820
Whatever the Bey says, nothing more.

460
00:51:43,820 --> 00:51:46,230
That's what our traditions say.

461
00:51:46,230 --> 00:51:49,670
Pity.

462
00:51:49,670 --> 00:51:54,180
Since when did you get old enough to
teach me our traditions, Zöhre?

463
00:51:57,100 --> 00:52:02,520
If you are to teach old Selcan the
traditions...

464
00:52:02,520 --> 00:52:05,540
... may Allah help those traditions.

465
00:52:05,590 --> 00:52:08,050
- We--
- You...

466
00:52:09,280 --> 00:52:13,910
... have confused shamelessness
with decency, my sweet girl.

467
00:52:18,590 --> 00:52:24,050
Now go with your mother, and think about
what you have done.

468
00:52:24,050 --> 00:52:28,360
Think, so that you can understand
how patient Selcan Hatun is.

469
00:52:29,260 --> 00:52:33,640
And about Bala Hatun. She is my guest.

470
00:52:36,440 --> 00:52:39,960
She is always welcome.

471
00:52:41,450 --> 00:52:49,100
If even the Bey himself comes, he can't touch
my guest without stepping on my dead body.

472
00:52:49,100 --> 00:52:52,510
Know that.

473
00:52:52,510 --> 00:52:56,460
Not enough? Tell your Bey the same thing.

474
00:52:58,760 --> 00:53:03,150
As you say, Hatun.

475
00:53:03,150 --> 00:53:05,810
Every man for himself.

476
00:53:05,810 --> 00:53:09,810
Expect yourself to be responsible for
what will happen to you from now on.

477
00:53:10,800 --> 00:53:13,300
Zöhre!

478
00:53:14,090 --> 00:53:16,950
I have two legs.

479
00:53:16,950 --> 00:53:23,080
Before I stumble on both of you, return
to your Tents.

480
00:53:26,540 --> 00:53:32,280
Don't make me boil! Leave with your
own will and...

481
00:53:32,280 --> 00:53:36,210
... don't make me kick you out.
Come on now!

482
00:54:36,240 --> 00:54:39,000
What was that?

483
00:54:40,170 --> 00:54:42,060
Come on.

484
00:54:43,740 --> 00:54:45,530
What's going on in there?

485
00:54:59,030 --> 00:55:01,550
Priest Marcus!

486
00:55:02,490 --> 00:55:06,490
How nice seeing you here once again!

487
00:55:07,510 --> 00:55:13,860
As long as you stay in these lands,
you'll see us every day.

488
00:55:14,860 --> 00:55:16,550
Where is the treasure?

489
00:55:16,550 --> 00:55:21,800
The thing that you call treasure, is
in one's heart, Yannis.

490
00:55:22,700 --> 00:55:25,780
No surprise that you look
for it so desperately.

491
00:55:38,380 --> 00:55:43,220
Does Edebali want Osman, or not?

492
00:55:44,400 --> 00:55:48,370
My master told me that he'll
give you what you want.

493
00:55:48,370 --> 00:55:50,790
Where is Edebali?

494
00:55:50,790 --> 00:55:54,930
He's waiting for you near Akçadede.

495
00:55:56,540 --> 00:56:02,530
But, if he doesn't see Osman
Bey alive and well...

496
00:56:02,530 --> 00:56:05,120
He will not be bringing the treasure.

497
00:56:05,120 --> 00:56:07,070
Megala!

498
00:56:10,580 --> 00:56:14,040
Take Osman to the place he's
talking about.

499
00:56:15,060 --> 00:56:18,140
I will be waiting for you there.

500
00:56:19,330 --> 00:56:25,940
If this is a trap, both Osman
and Edebali will die.

501
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:02,150
Faster you idiots!

502
00:57:28,540 --> 00:57:31,860
You're finally mine, Osman Bey.

503
00:57:33,100 --> 00:57:36,920
You tricked us! You dog!

504
00:57:37,350 --> 00:57:41,350
I'll kill you just like that Kanturalı
you have sent to kill me.

505
00:57:42,930 --> 00:57:44,440
Kanturalı!

506
00:57:44,440 --> 00:57:48,380
Dogs like you cannot bite Kanturalı!

507
00:57:50,990 --> 00:57:54,310
Dündar Bey's foolish son Batur...

508
00:57:55,520 --> 00:57:57,610
He wants your head.

509
00:58:00,300 --> 00:58:02,180
Batur?

510
00:58:03,600 --> 00:58:09,730
Not only you, your dogs around
you also fear me to death.

511
00:58:10,550 --> 00:58:13,600
I see it in their eyes.

512
00:58:16,870 --> 00:58:19,590
Your death will be fun.

513
00:58:32,010 --> 00:58:34,340
Allah almighty!

514
00:58:45,600 --> 00:58:47,700
I'm here cousin!

515
00:58:51,740 --> 00:58:53,750
Die!

516
00:58:55,470 --> 00:58:57,320
Batur!

517
00:59:29,990 --> 00:59:31,690
Konur Alp!

518
00:59:33,360 --> 00:59:37,950
Show no mercy! Hit them hard! No mercy!

519
00:59:37,950 --> 00:59:41,590
Bamsı Bey! Sergeant Samsa!

520
00:59:41,860 --> 00:59:46,570
- Allah is eternal!
- Allah is eternal!

521
01:00:04,870 --> 01:00:07,220
Brother!

522
01:00:09,130 --> 01:00:14,110
Batur! What should I say, you came
right on time.

523
01:00:14,110 --> 01:00:17,850
- Thank you.
- How did you find this place?

524
01:00:17,850 --> 01:00:23,580
Juan fell into my trap.
He brought me to you, brother.

525
01:00:24,880 --> 01:00:27,680
Bless you.

526
01:00:28,540 --> 01:00:31,170
Bless you too.

527
01:00:40,440 --> 01:00:45,350
Thank you Batur Bey.
You played those devil's sons good.

528
01:00:47,390 --> 01:00:49,960
Brother!

529
01:00:51,500 --> 01:00:55,090
Brother!

530
01:01:00,330 --> 01:01:03,300
Thank Allah!

531
01:01:11,420 --> 01:01:13,880
Samsa!

532
01:01:40,690 --> 01:01:43,070
Bamsı Bey!

533
01:01:51,160 --> 01:01:53,550
Boğaç!

534
01:01:54,980 --> 01:01:57,560
He's not doing good.

535
01:02:09,670 --> 01:02:14,100
- Osman!
- Abdurrahman Gazi!

536
01:02:47,800 --> 01:02:51,800
Thank Allah!
So that means my father is back!

537
01:03:19,900 --> 01:03:24,770
Brother! My father...

538
01:03:32,050 --> 01:03:36,330
Abdurrahman Gazi, where is my father?

539
01:03:39,490 --> 01:03:42,470
Please tell me! Where is my father?

540
01:03:47,160 --> 01:03:50,150
Our father is sick, brother.

541
01:03:56,070 --> 01:04:01,590
From now on, our Bey is uncle Dündar.

542
01:04:37,650 --> 01:04:40,660
How the years pass by!

543
01:04:42,650 --> 01:04:47,910
The shining face of my Hayma ana, the rich
sound of my Süleyman Şah!

544
01:04:48,000 --> 01:04:51,520
My little Osman's naughty behaviors.

545
01:04:55,100 --> 01:04:58,140
Sit here, I'll show you something.

546
01:05:04,120 --> 01:05:08,120
These are Osman's. Look!

547
01:05:08,300 --> 01:05:10,130
His sweater.

548
01:05:10,980 --> 01:05:14,470
- So small!
- Right? So small.

549
01:05:14,470 --> 01:05:18,120
He was a lion back then, he's a lion now.

550
01:05:18,300 --> 01:05:22,200
I knitted that lions first mane.

551
01:05:24,980 --> 01:05:31,520
He grew up, bloomed, used swords
with Bamsı Bey, Turgut Bey.

552
01:05:32,500 --> 01:05:38,840
Allah made him a valiant, his father
Ertuğrul Bey made him a master swordsman.

553
01:05:42,990 --> 01:05:46,990
He would always shine among
all the children in the Tent!

554
01:05:48,060 --> 01:05:52,300
His arrow was the first to hit, he was
the first to leave the wooden sword!

555
01:05:54,130 --> 01:05:58,030
His peers always followed him.

556
01:05:58,030 --> 01:06:03,800
He grew up and became a Bey.
His friends became Alps.

557
01:06:04,850 --> 01:06:08,430
Thankfully they never got separated.

558
01:06:12,480 --> 01:06:17,450
Selcan Hatun. There is
something I'm wondering.

559
01:06:18,100 --> 01:06:20,470
Ask me, my girl.

560
01:06:25,280 --> 01:06:28,520
Come on ask me, don't be shy.

561
01:06:30,960 --> 01:06:33,630
Osman Bey...

562
01:06:34,680 --> 01:06:38,050
Has he fallen in love before?

563
01:06:45,750 --> 01:06:48,640
I wouldn't know that, my girl.

564
01:06:49,160 --> 01:06:53,630
But I know how the light in his
eyes shine when I say Bala.

565
01:06:55,040 --> 01:06:59,040
I'm Osman's mother. I know him well.

566
01:06:59,160 --> 01:07:03,740
If I was a mother for him, you
should know this.

567
01:07:03,740 --> 01:07:07,360
Bala Hatun is written in Osman's heart.

568
01:07:09,090 --> 01:07:14,390
I know it from how his voice thrills, how
his eyes shine when I say Bala Hatun.

569
01:07:16,890 --> 01:07:19,640
Just like yours.

570
01:07:20,180 --> 01:07:24,320
It seems to me that my Allah has tied
your hearts together.

571
01:07:24,320 --> 01:07:28,120
- I hope for the best about you.
- Allah willing.

572
01:07:28,540 --> 01:07:30,730
Allah willing!

573
01:08:09,420 --> 01:08:11,650
Osman Bey is coming!

574
01:08:14,040 --> 01:08:16,300
Thank Allah!

575
01:08:17,100 --> 01:08:19,540
Thank heavens!

576
01:08:23,060 --> 01:08:36,010
www.Kurulusosman.online

577
01:09:45,980 --> 01:09:51,050
My Allah brought you back to us, Osman.

578
01:10:48,070 --> 01:10:51,260
Thank you, uncle.

579
01:11:01,280 --> 01:11:05,280
You made me very proud.

580
01:11:05,980 --> 01:11:09,980
You saved Osman with the help of Allah.

581
01:11:10,960 --> 01:11:14,960
Thank you, my son, thank you.

582
01:11:15,750 --> 01:11:39,650
Long live Batur Alp!

583
01:11:46,310 --> 01:11:48,870
May Allah bless you, cousin.

584
01:11:51,190 --> 01:11:53,060
You too, cousin.

585
01:12:16,400 --> 01:12:22,660
Thank you, Dündar Bey, for these problems
that have been burning our hearts are solved.

586
01:12:22,920 --> 01:12:27,850
But we wonder, how could
Batur Alp handle this?

587
01:12:33,940 --> 01:12:38,420
By using his head, Selcan
Hatun, by using his head.

588
01:12:38,690 --> 01:12:42,130
I have the key to save Osman, father.

589
01:12:42,290 --> 01:12:47,370
Also, if we save him, your Beyhood
in the Tent will be reinforced.

590
01:12:47,820 --> 01:12:51,230
- How?
- I have that man called Juan.

591
01:12:51,880 --> 01:12:53,830
He will take us to Osman.

592
01:12:54,130 --> 01:12:57,340
Attack there with Bamsı Bey then.

593
01:13:00,230 --> 01:13:01,350
Zöhre.

594
01:13:01,970 --> 01:13:04,840
I can take care of my Osman.

595
01:13:09,300 --> 01:13:10,740
Aunt.

596
01:13:15,010 --> 01:13:19,010
May those who did this to you be
drowned in their own blood, son.

597
01:13:22,860 --> 01:13:26,860
Osman, when you feel better...

598
01:13:27,720 --> 01:13:29,230
... come to the tent.

599
01:13:30,550 --> 01:13:32,300
Will do, uncle.

600
01:13:33,950 --> 01:13:35,030
Will do.

601
01:13:40,950 --> 01:13:41,960
Osman.

602
01:13:43,960 --> 01:13:48,030
- Bala Hatun is in the Tent.
- Is she, aunt?

603
01:13:48,330 --> 01:13:51,250
- Go.
- Thank you.

604
01:14:26,460 --> 01:14:27,890
Prisoners escaped.

605
01:14:28,970 --> 01:14:30,980
Master Yannis.

606
01:14:33,690 --> 01:14:35,310
We are leaving!

607
01:15:06,400 --> 01:15:08,500
I got out of hell...

608
01:15:09,810 --> 01:15:11,650
... and came to you.

609
01:15:13,130 --> 01:15:17,310
My Allah granted me
the heaven, Bala Hatun.

610
01:15:18,480 --> 01:15:21,090
I begged for every second.

611
01:15:21,670 --> 01:15:25,670
Thank Allah, you are here, safe and sound.

612
01:15:26,020 --> 01:15:29,360
Allah made me the
happiest person, Osman Bey.

613
01:15:42,640 --> 01:15:44,870
But you are exhausted.

614
01:15:46,860 --> 01:15:51,350
May the hands of those who did these to
you be broken, may their bloodline perish!

615
01:15:52,410 --> 01:15:56,410
- You should be in the healing tent.
- Don't you know...

616
01:15:58,150 --> 01:16:01,990
... that your words are
medicine for my wounds.

617
01:16:03,110 --> 01:16:05,810
Your eyes are the light that
shine through my nights.

618
01:16:07,520 --> 01:16:11,930
I have forgotten my pains now.

619
01:16:14,380 --> 01:16:16,120
You should forget them too.

620
01:16:19,140 --> 01:16:28,460
"Indeed, Allah is with the patient."
Surah Al-Baqarah [2:153]

621
01:16:55,330 --> 01:16:57,560
Where is this Edebali?

622
01:17:00,420 --> 01:17:02,370
Or is this a game too?

623
01:17:02,450 --> 01:17:06,450
I assure you, that my
master sees you, Yannis.

624
01:17:35,910 --> 01:17:37,200
Edebali.

625
01:18:13,070 --> 01:18:14,280
Soldiers!

626
01:18:32,810 --> 01:18:35,520
All those years have worn you, Edebali.

627
01:18:36,780 --> 01:18:40,780
From the young boy that
I saw in the Âhi Evran...

628
01:18:40,830 --> 01:18:43,070
... to this old man.

629
01:18:43,410 --> 01:18:45,890
It depends on how you look at it, Yannis.

630
01:18:46,700 --> 01:18:50,700
I am young enough to
fight you at all times...

631
01:18:54,890 --> 01:18:57,900
... and old enough
to die at any time.

632
01:18:59,640 --> 01:19:03,400
It seems these nonsenses
didn't help you.

633
01:19:03,770 --> 01:19:05,180
Here you are.

634
01:19:10,470 --> 01:19:14,510
And you know you will die if
you don't give me what I want.

635
01:19:15,170 --> 01:19:21,680
Those who die for their cause live longer
than their executioners, Yannis.

636
01:19:22,620 --> 01:19:24,740
You are not going to give up, are you?

637
01:19:25,930 --> 01:19:29,930
That fighter spirit in you makes
you stubborn like a goat.

638
01:19:30,430 --> 01:19:33,560
You can't even see the
defeat coming at your door.

639
01:19:37,100 --> 01:19:40,390
Allah ordered us to
fight with the tyrants.

640
01:19:40,910 --> 01:19:43,420
Allah is the one who
gives victory or defeat.

641
01:19:44,040 --> 01:19:48,180
We will accept whatever
outcome Allah shows us.

642
01:19:52,010 --> 01:19:58,320
Pity, such a pity that you still believe
you can change the system I built.

643
01:19:59,240 --> 01:20:04,510
Not just the system, we will
change the era, Yannis.

644
01:20:06,660 --> 01:20:11,210
This reign of tyranny you have
built will be destroyed.

645
01:20:50,240 --> 01:20:52,750
The great...

646
01:20:54,110 --> 01:20:56,720
... Osman...

647
01:20:58,220 --> 01:21:00,250
... the grandchild of Süleyman Shah.

648
01:21:10,270 --> 01:21:15,120
Look at your wounds very carefully.

649
01:21:18,010 --> 01:21:20,310
Look at your wounds...

650
01:21:21,990 --> 01:21:24,210
... so that you can see your tomorrow.

651
01:21:37,270 --> 01:21:41,100
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
[In the name of God, the merciful and compassionate.]

652
01:22:03,690 --> 01:22:07,690
Let your wounds burn you, Osman Bey.

653
01:22:08,010 --> 01:22:10,040
Let them burn...

654
01:22:13,120 --> 01:22:15,640
... so your flame keeps getting stronger.

655
01:22:41,570 --> 01:22:45,090
Let them hurt you, Osman Bey.

656
01:22:47,480 --> 01:22:49,720
Let them hurt...

657
01:22:50,910 --> 01:22:53,820
... so you know where you stand.

658
01:22:55,720 --> 01:22:58,160
Things that are done to you...

659
01:22:59,780 --> 01:23:03,020
... are the signs of what
you will do to them.

660
01:23:04,520 --> 01:23:06,620
Don't you forget that.

661
01:23:08,640 --> 01:23:10,670
Don't you forget that.

662
01:23:26,070 --> 01:23:28,250
You haven't changed at all.

663
01:23:28,360 --> 01:23:31,300
Now that we are waiting for
the treasure and Osman...

664
01:23:31,370 --> 01:23:36,700
... I would want to hear how you trained
these men that are loyal to you to death.

665
01:23:49,110 --> 01:23:52,640
Our hearts are in the
hands of Allah, Yannis.

666
01:23:53,220 --> 01:23:56,310
It is impossible to see this
light, understand this...

667
01:23:56,700 --> 01:24:00,480
... loyalty from the well of
infidelity that you fell in.

668
01:24:02,240 --> 01:24:04,130
I infiltrated right next to you.

669
01:24:04,460 --> 01:24:09,780
I've trained hundreds of men
that are loyal to us in the soul.

670
01:24:10,450 --> 01:24:13,990
The sense of unity of
the Muslims are over, Edebali.

671
01:24:14,150 --> 01:24:16,900
You can believe you'll
resurrect that soul.

672
01:24:17,050 --> 01:24:21,260
I will gather new souls with the
gold that I will take from you.

673
01:24:21,430 --> 01:24:25,130
I will hit you with the ones
who were with you.

674
01:24:27,480 --> 01:24:30,670
There are such brave ones between us...

675
01:24:30,960 --> 01:24:33,770
... that their souls
are priceless, Yannis.

676
01:24:34,050 --> 01:24:38,700
Neither ranks, gold, nor
any other mortal things.

677
01:24:39,350 --> 01:24:46,720
They feed with Dhikr, wear gratitude,
and fight with patience.

678
01:24:46,880 --> 01:24:52,930
But you aren't even aware of this,
because you are a pawn of your devil.

679
01:24:53,250 --> 01:24:57,780
Don't forget that the devil's
former name was Azazel.

680
01:24:59,990 --> 01:25:04,180
Guardian of Heaven, and teacher of angels.

681
01:25:05,000 --> 01:25:07,100
You share the same fate.

682
01:25:07,750 --> 01:25:13,290
Your passion for victory, and
pride is making you a devil.

683
01:25:13,530 --> 01:25:16,650
If it's the victory in the
end, I don't care at all!

684
01:25:18,100 --> 01:25:22,750
But I wonder, why is Osman
so important to you?

685
01:25:25,860 --> 01:25:30,510
Are you planning to give the wooden
sword of Ahmet Yesevî's to him?

686
01:25:31,030 --> 01:25:35,030
Fate is making its nets, Yannis.

687
01:25:35,200 --> 01:25:39,970
Brave people like Osman
will end people like you.

688
01:25:41,910 --> 01:25:43,490
Osman.

689
01:25:45,260 --> 01:25:48,200
My Batur, my valiant son...

690
01:25:48,480 --> 01:25:52,750
May Allah help you and make
your sword sharp at all times.

691
01:25:54,180 --> 01:25:56,880
Amin, mother, thank you.

692
01:25:57,610 --> 01:26:01,610
Everything has changed in the Tent.

693
01:26:02,180 --> 01:26:06,560
May Allah grant all
fathers a son like you.

694
01:26:07,820 --> 01:26:10,000
I would die in your path, father.

695
01:26:18,470 --> 01:26:21,580
Edebali sent his daughter to the Tent.

696
01:26:22,260 --> 01:26:26,260
You should get Edebali away
from Osman, Dündar Bey.

697
01:26:26,950 --> 01:26:29,800
Or we will have more
trouble in the future.

698
01:26:30,030 --> 01:26:34,030
Is the girl in Osman's tent now?

699
01:26:34,420 --> 01:26:35,630
Yes, father.

700
01:26:36,820 --> 01:26:40,990
I fear that she wants to marry
Osman and settle in the Tent.

701
01:26:42,820 --> 01:26:46,000
That would be the end of Kayı Tent.

702
01:26:46,240 --> 01:26:49,260
Come on, come with me!

703
01:26:51,510 --> 01:26:55,110
Let's see what they are up to.

704
01:27:08,250 --> 01:27:11,010
- Thank you, Aybüke.
- Enjoy.

705
01:27:12,420 --> 01:27:14,060
Thank you.

706
01:27:17,800 --> 01:27:19,290
Thank you.

707
01:27:24,640 --> 01:27:27,740
Thank Allah, our Tent
is peaceful again.

708
01:27:27,880 --> 01:27:28,960
Thank Allah.

709
01:27:29,300 --> 01:27:34,290
Now, If I make my Osman marry
too, I can die in peace.

710
01:27:50,040 --> 01:27:51,670
What is it, Dündar Bey?

711
01:27:54,630 --> 01:27:58,360
I've heard that Bala Hatun is here.

712
01:27:59,070 --> 01:28:02,670
I want to talk with her about that.

713
01:28:05,360 --> 01:28:07,360
Why did she come to the Tent?

714
01:28:07,530 --> 01:28:11,530
Are those things that happened
have a connection with Edebali?

715
01:28:14,040 --> 01:28:19,190
Tell me, girl, how could
your father contact Alps?

716
01:28:19,990 --> 01:28:21,850
He saw them in his dream.

717
01:28:35,250 --> 01:28:38,760
So, he saw them in his dream.

718
01:28:41,300 --> 01:28:45,890
If he only could see them earlier,
Osman wouldn't be attacked.

719
01:28:47,580 --> 01:28:50,350
Allah is the one who saves and destroys.

720
01:28:51,460 --> 01:28:53,640
Bala Hatun says what she knows.

721
01:28:55,400 --> 01:28:58,800
What, you also don't
believe in dreams now?

722
01:29:00,430 --> 01:29:02,890
You can talk about this with my father.

723
01:29:03,420 --> 01:29:06,640
Thank Allah for giving
Osman back to you.

724
01:29:07,710 --> 01:29:09,310
Thank Allah.

725
01:29:10,000 --> 01:29:11,810
Thank Allah he's returned.

726
01:29:12,280 --> 01:29:18,770
But how could we know whether this fight
tries to kill him, or someone we know...

727
01:29:19,680 --> 01:29:20,730
... again?

728
01:29:21,200 --> 01:29:25,200
We were living in peace
and unity in this Tent.

729
01:29:25,380 --> 01:29:29,380
All these troubles emerged
with the arrival of Edebali.

730
01:29:29,530 --> 01:29:33,730
- Uncle.
- I am talking Osman, I am!

731
01:29:35,870 --> 01:29:38,730
Bey of the Tent!

732
01:29:42,430 --> 01:29:43,650
Now...

733
01:29:45,250 --> 01:29:49,250
... hear what I will say.

734
01:29:50,200 --> 01:29:55,000
I don't want unity in
this Tent to be deformed.

735
01:29:57,740 --> 01:30:02,950
I don't want people
causing trouble in my Tent.

736
01:30:10,930 --> 01:30:12,720
We did not see...

737
01:30:13,440 --> 01:30:16,710
... scattering and being
ruined from our ancestors.

738
01:30:17,840 --> 01:30:21,840
We saw helping each other, and being one.

739
01:30:23,960 --> 01:30:27,690
Leave us alone from now on, Bala Hatun.

740
01:30:28,670 --> 01:30:34,410
That is enough, we do not want
any more trouble and curse.

741
01:30:39,010 --> 01:30:43,010
Now to you, Osman. If you continue to...

742
01:30:43,220 --> 01:30:50,050
... work with that Edebali, know that
you will not get our help anymore.

743
01:30:57,070 --> 01:30:58,960
I understand, Dündar Bey.

744
01:30:59,670 --> 01:31:03,490
May Allah keep you away from
any kind of trouble and curse.

745
01:31:08,350 --> 01:31:09,950
If you'll excuse me.

746
01:31:11,190 --> 01:31:12,920
Come on, Gonca Hatun.

747
01:31:45,330 --> 01:31:46,430
Osman.

748
01:31:48,950 --> 01:31:51,000
You endured many troubles.

749
01:31:51,280 --> 01:31:55,950
But now is the time to
make up your own mind.

750
01:31:56,580 --> 01:32:04,040
Edebali, his daughter, and his dervishes
brought nothing but trouble into this Tent.

751
01:32:04,850 --> 01:32:08,580
Bala Hatun has no place in this Tent.

752
01:32:08,900 --> 01:32:09,930
Uncle!

753
01:32:11,360 --> 01:32:13,080
What are you saying?

754
01:32:14,660 --> 01:32:18,560
Sofia held the dagger that
opened my wounds.

755
01:32:19,340 --> 01:32:21,990
Trouble is coming from the infidels!

756
01:32:23,160 --> 01:32:27,960
Neither Sheikh Edebali nor his
daughter had anything to do with it.

757
01:32:29,140 --> 01:32:30,290
On the contrary.

758
01:32:31,560 --> 01:32:34,040
We highly value them.

759
01:32:41,010 --> 01:32:42,420
Osman.

760
01:32:43,390 --> 01:32:46,300
You are at the crossroads now, Osman.

761
01:32:46,710 --> 01:32:50,960
This Tent is the place you belong to.

762
01:32:51,830 --> 01:32:54,330
Know who you rebel for.

763
01:32:55,480 --> 01:32:56,240
I...

764
01:32:57,980 --> 01:33:00,560
... wouldn't just rebel for her.

765
01:33:01,700 --> 01:33:05,700
I would be a sword and
strike if necessary!

766
01:33:13,170 --> 01:33:14,690
And you...

767
01:33:15,780 --> 01:33:17,950
... should know it like this.

768
01:33:31,020 --> 01:33:32,220
Bala Hatun!

769
01:33:32,420 --> 01:33:33,370
Bala Hatun!

770
01:33:35,580 --> 01:33:36,660
Bala Hatun!

771
01:33:40,580 --> 01:33:41,940
Calm down.

772
01:33:45,020 --> 01:33:48,240
Even if the whole world
try to take you from me...

773
01:33:48,560 --> 01:33:50,420
... I would bow before no one!

774
01:33:50,830 --> 01:33:55,650
I know, Osman, but no one should
be in trouble because of us.

775
01:33:56,040 --> 01:34:00,680
No one should be without their homes,
Ahîs can't stay out of trouble.

776
01:34:01,010 --> 01:34:05,670
I would die for the trouble
that's coming from you, Bala Hatun.

777
01:34:06,870 --> 01:34:10,440
Tell me, where is Edebali?

778
01:34:12,390 --> 01:34:15,900
I will send my Selcan aunt
and ask to marry you.

779
01:34:22,930 --> 01:34:24,740
He went to the Ahîs.

780
01:34:25,040 --> 01:34:26,780
He went to the Ahîs?

781
01:34:28,110 --> 01:34:30,110
Then what are you doing here?

782
01:34:31,530 --> 01:34:34,330
My father thought that
would be best, Osman Bey.

783
01:34:34,970 --> 01:34:35,960
Bala Hatun.

784
01:34:37,800 --> 01:34:39,770
Tell me, what are you hiding from me?

785
01:34:41,160 --> 01:34:43,570
I can't tell you this, Osman Bey!

786
01:34:47,260 --> 01:34:48,610
Bala Hatun.

787
01:34:49,410 --> 01:34:51,200
Why can't you tell me, Bala Hatun?

788
01:34:51,770 --> 01:34:54,820
I can't, you are the future of this Tent.

789
01:34:55,780 --> 01:34:58,220
I wouldn't want you to be in more trouble.

790
01:34:58,590 --> 01:35:00,420
My father wouldn't want that either.

791
01:35:01,190 --> 01:35:02,620
Now, let me go.

792
01:35:03,090 --> 01:35:03,950
Come on!

793
01:35:04,160 --> 01:35:05,030
Bala!

794
01:35:08,810 --> 01:35:12,810
Now you are telling me
where your father is!

795
01:35:13,570 --> 01:35:14,940
What is going on?

796
01:35:15,540 --> 01:35:20,390
If you don't tell me the truth,
you can't get out of this Tent.

797
01:35:27,870 --> 01:35:28,830
My father...

798
01:35:30,450 --> 01:35:33,190
... he sent me here after he
heard what happened to you.

799
01:35:33,490 --> 01:35:36,610
I understood that he is going
to sacrifice himself for you.

800
01:35:47,300 --> 01:35:48,440
Then...

801
01:35:53,840 --> 01:35:55,320
... Yannis has him.

802
01:35:55,570 --> 01:35:58,710
He is going to give Yannis
the treasure for you, Osman Bey.

803
01:35:59,140 --> 01:36:00,730
How could he do this?

804
01:36:03,080 --> 01:36:05,120
Do you know where he went?

805
01:36:06,670 --> 01:36:09,060
Believe me, he didn't say
to me either, Osman Bey.

806
01:36:11,120 --> 01:36:14,170
I still remember his words before leaving.

807
01:36:14,790 --> 01:36:18,230
He said, " We came from the soil,
we will return to the soil."

808
01:36:27,440 --> 01:36:31,710
Remove the clay, give it to the treasure.

809
01:36:32,300 --> 01:36:34,580
Sheikh Edebali.

810
01:36:36,190 --> 01:36:37,150
I know.

811
01:36:38,990 --> 01:36:40,970
I know where he is.

812
01:36:42,640 --> 01:36:47,950
Stop worrying, Bala Hatun,
I know where your father is.

813
01:36:48,210 --> 01:36:49,290
How?

814
01:36:50,460 --> 01:36:53,740
First, I will save Sheikh Edebali
from those infidels...

815
01:36:54,030 --> 01:36:56,410
... then I will ask him to
let me marry you.

816
01:37:00,910 --> 01:37:04,910
After we get over this too, we
will be happy if Allah permits.

817
01:37:13,190 --> 01:37:15,760
You have ruined everything.

818
01:37:16,230 --> 01:37:19,780
You can't even be
satisfied with your victory.

819
01:37:21,810 --> 01:37:26,830
As long as this woman is with
you, your Tent won't be peaceful.

820
01:37:28,370 --> 01:37:30,490
What is it, Selcan Hatun?

821
01:37:31,840 --> 01:37:34,060
Are you trying to end my marriage?

822
01:37:35,300 --> 01:37:39,110
No, I am trying to save the Kayı Tent.

823
01:37:39,360 --> 01:37:40,840
Aunt Selcan.

824
01:37:42,370 --> 01:37:46,110
You came here as a guest. We are honored.

825
01:37:46,890 --> 01:37:50,890
But don't try to meddle with
the business of this Tent.

826
01:37:52,030 --> 01:37:56,530
Or I will have to end your visit here.

827
01:38:01,370 --> 01:38:06,200
When you are a Bey, you will
rule over someone eventually.

828
01:38:10,360 --> 01:38:14,360
But don't you forget.
You are not a Bey.

829
01:38:14,370 --> 01:38:16,320
You are just a deputy.

830
01:39:56,510 --> 01:39:57,660
They've escaped.

831
01:40:15,210 --> 01:40:16,870
Where is Osman, Megala?

832
01:40:17,770 --> 01:40:19,240
They've escaped, sir.

833
01:40:19,980 --> 01:40:22,110
They also killed all of our men.

834
01:40:31,400 --> 01:40:34,070
Attack! Kill them all!

835
01:41:07,170 --> 01:41:08,370
Osman!

836
01:41:09,080 --> 01:41:10,850
I am here, my Sheikh!

837
01:41:21,320 --> 01:41:22,630
Master Yannis!

838
01:41:26,200 --> 01:41:28,590
Master, they outnumbered
us, we have to go now!

839
01:41:32,160 --> 01:41:34,040
You go, I will distract them.

840
01:43:20,380 --> 01:43:24,400
No.
You should turn it a little bit more.

841
01:43:26,870 --> 01:43:31,160
Look at my Bala.
How excited she is!

842
01:43:31,190 --> 01:43:35,200
It's good now.
You're pretty, Masha Allah (praise be).

843
01:43:35,890 --> 01:43:39,880
We have gone through a lot of troubles.

844
01:43:39,880 --> 01:43:44,420
We have risen from the dead.
However...

845
01:43:44,460 --> 01:43:46,830
I have never been more excited, Gonca.

846
01:43:46,850 --> 01:43:51,340
My Lord has gifted you with love,
that's why, Bala Hatun.

847
01:43:51,400 --> 01:43:56,690
- May it continue like this, in sha Allah.
- In sha Allah (if Allah permits).

848
01:43:58,430 --> 01:44:01,180
Selcan Hatun will be here soon.

849
01:44:02,970 --> 01:44:07,010
My Allah, may you gift me with calmness.

850
01:44:07,850 --> 01:44:12,570
You are a rose that has not been
bloomed yet in your father's garden, Bala.

851
01:44:12,850 --> 01:44:15,120
You are his precious one.

852
01:44:17,480 --> 01:44:22,010
I don't know if my sheik gives you to
Osman Bey.

853
01:44:22,970 --> 01:44:27,930
My father abandoned the treasure for
Osman Bey.

854
01:44:27,990 --> 01:44:30,300
He has risked his own life.

855
01:44:30,510 --> 01:44:33,000
His feelings about Osman is clear.

856
01:44:33,200 --> 01:44:36,160
This marriage will satisfy him too.

857
01:44:36,530 --> 01:44:41,160
You are right. My sheik keeps
talking about Osman Bey's braveness.

858
01:44:41,160 --> 01:44:42,830
He trusts him.

859
01:44:42,850 --> 01:44:46,290
He wouldn't entrust you to anyone but him.

860
01:44:46,800 --> 01:44:49,820
Then, tell me.

861
01:44:49,820 --> 01:44:54,820
What do you want first?
A girl or a boy?

862
01:44:55,570 --> 01:44:58,450
I just want a propitious child.

863
01:44:58,690 --> 01:45:02,940
May our Lord give us the best.

864
01:45:03,020 --> 01:45:05,650
- In sha Allah.
- In sha Allah.

865
01:45:08,650 --> 01:45:13,710
You have fought for us
and face death.

866
01:45:13,780 --> 01:45:15,900
Live long, Osman Bey.

867
01:45:15,900 --> 01:45:18,220
I girt on.
But, I heard that...

868
01:45:18,580 --> 01:45:24,030
you risked your life for me, Edebalı.

869
01:45:26,040 --> 01:45:30,880
They tortured you.
How did you manage to save yourself?

870
01:45:31,110 --> 01:45:37,790
I got out of that dark well thanks to
your light, Edebalı.

871
01:45:42,940 --> 01:45:47,710
It's not about looking, it's about
seeing, son.

872
01:45:47,710 --> 01:45:52,200
As you can see it, that light
is inside you.

873
01:45:52,910 --> 01:45:57,960
In sha Allah, that light will brighten
Oghuz's horizon.

874
01:45:59,320 --> 01:46:03,310
Then, what about the darkness in my heart,
Edebalı?

875
01:46:04,270 --> 01:46:07,590
Why did you refuse me when I came
to you?

876
01:46:10,210 --> 01:46:16,150
That you refused me hurt me a lot.

877
01:46:17,220 --> 01:46:20,870
Excuse my naiveness.

878
01:46:24,310 --> 01:46:26,920
Forgive me, Edebalı.

879
01:46:29,120 --> 01:46:31,470
My Sheik, Edebalı.

880
01:46:36,970 --> 01:46:40,430
I am not the one to forgive.

881
01:46:42,080 --> 01:46:50,910
But, I know that the one who knows his
mistakes is on the right path, son.

882
01:46:52,040 --> 01:46:56,810
Your path is good, so is your intention.

883
01:46:58,220 --> 01:47:04,770
Just preserve yourself, and protect your
heart.

884
01:47:19,480 --> 01:47:21,160
Father.

885
01:47:30,580 --> 01:47:32,490
Who did this to you?

886
01:47:32,500 --> 01:47:35,760
Osman!
Osman!

887
01:48:03,700 --> 01:48:06,620
Call a doctor. Now!

888
01:48:19,160 --> 01:48:21,120
Megela...

889
01:48:22,750 --> 01:48:25,220
Megela is dead, my daughter.

890
01:48:25,430 --> 01:48:27,970
Don't panic, sir.

891
01:48:28,530 --> 01:48:31,560
We will take revenge.

892
01:48:40,130 --> 01:48:42,140
What happened?

893
01:48:44,060 --> 01:48:46,240
Where is Edebalı?

894
01:48:47,150 --> 01:48:49,710
Where is Osman?

895
01:48:49,760 --> 01:48:52,890
Everything is obvious now.

896
01:48:52,940 --> 01:48:58,610
My daughter, from now on,
it's just about blood!

897
01:49:07,540 --> 01:49:10,070
Sir Yannis.

898
01:49:11,080 --> 01:49:14,810
Juan died because of his foolishness.

899
01:49:14,810 --> 01:49:17,100
What about you, Salvador?

900
01:49:20,300 --> 01:49:24,280
What are you going to do about your
clumsiness?

901
01:49:35,340 --> 01:49:39,430
It was an unlucky situation of Juan,
Kalanoz.

902
01:49:40,020 --> 01:49:44,780
In fact, in Kulucahisar Castle, clumsy
ones are more precious.

903
01:49:44,780 --> 01:49:49,070
- What do you mean, Salvador?
- It's clear.

904
01:49:50,280 --> 01:49:53,870
While I was out there fighting with
my men, you...

905
01:49:53,870 --> 01:49:55,750
Enough!

906
01:50:17,290 --> 01:50:21,120
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
[in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.]

907
01:50:26,610 --> 01:50:29,020
I have freshened up.

908
01:50:30,590 --> 01:50:36,270
- You made this.
- Yes, father. May it heal you.

909
01:50:37,180 --> 01:50:41,350
It tastes like your deceased Mother's
Rose Sherbet (beverage).

910
01:50:42,170 --> 01:50:45,750
May my Lord gift her grave with glory,
in sha Allah.

911
01:50:45,770 --> 01:50:47,810
In sha Allah.

912
01:50:49,140 --> 01:50:53,950
What a wonderful daughter you left for me
Ulduz Hatun.

913
01:50:54,940 --> 01:50:59,830
May Allah gift you with his merciness.

914
01:51:00,990 --> 01:51:05,770
How are you, father?
A lot happened, I couldn't ask you.

915
01:51:06,900 --> 01:51:14,090
Osman Bey is free.
The treasure is safe now, thank Allah.

916
01:51:14,100 --> 01:51:16,040
Thank Allah.

917
01:51:16,040 --> 01:51:21,270
But, there are so many troubles waiting
for Osman.

918
01:51:22,270 --> 01:51:26,610
- May my Lord help him.
- Amin.

919
01:51:29,600 --> 01:51:31,450
Father.

920
01:51:32,260 --> 01:51:36,870
I want to tell you something,
but I feel shy.

921
01:51:41,070 --> 01:51:45,780
Don't be shy, my beautiful daughter.
Tell me.

922
01:51:45,810 --> 01:51:47,920
Osman Bey.

923
01:51:50,660 --> 01:51:52,940
Osman Bey told me...

924
01:51:56,950 --> 01:52:01,730
Tell me, daughter.
What did Osman Bey tell you?

925
01:52:04,600 --> 01:52:07,710
He will send Selcan Hatun.

926
01:52:08,930 --> 01:52:11,860
To ask for me in marriage.

927
01:52:17,440 --> 01:52:26,090
Say, "He will give them life who produced
them the first time;

928
01:52:26,090 --> 01:52:30,910
...and He is, of all creation, Knowing."

929
01:52:31,050 --> 01:52:44,330
[It is] He who made for you from the green
tree, fire, and then from it you ignite.

930
01:52:44,370 --> 01:52:55,710
Is not He who created the heavens and the
earth Able to create the likes of them?

931
01:52:55,710 --> 01:53:01,990
Yes, [it is so]; and He is the Knowing Creator.

932
01:53:02,040 --> 01:53:15,350
His command is only when He intends a
thing that He says to it, "Be," and it is.

933
01:53:15,350 --> 01:53:29,750
So exalted is He in whose hand is the realm
of all things, and to Him you will be returned.
[Yasin Surah 19-23]

934
01:53:29,980 --> 01:53:38,500
"Glory to thy Lord the Lord, of Honour and Power! (He is free) from what they ascribe (to Him)! And Peace on the Messengers!

935
01:53:38,660 --> 01:53:45,150
And praise to Allah, the Lord and Cherisher of the Worlds." (Surah as-Saaffat, 180-182)

936
01:53:46,100 --> 01:53:56,990
Reciting Surah Al-Fatiha (The Opening) [1]

937
01:54:21,630 --> 01:54:24,240
My martyred...

938
01:54:24,840 --> 01:54:27,220
brother.

939
01:54:30,080 --> 01:54:34,770
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
[in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.]

940
01:54:44,610 --> 01:54:46,950
Demirbüken.

941
01:54:54,610 --> 01:54:56,850
Brothers...

942
01:54:58,610 --> 01:55:01,390
We will take your revenge.

943
01:55:03,790 --> 01:55:05,840
We will.

944
01:55:14,200 --> 01:55:17,710
They will be drowned in the blood they
shed, brother.

945
01:55:19,020 --> 01:55:21,790
We will take revenge.

946
01:55:22,070 --> 01:55:23,630
We will.

947
01:55:40,940 --> 01:55:45,420
To make this land our home...

948
01:55:45,420 --> 01:55:51,370
so many valiants have died.

949
01:55:58,230 --> 01:56:08,390
So many fathers buried their sons
with their own hands.

950
01:56:13,660 --> 01:56:17,590
Their lovers have been abandoned.

951
01:56:18,060 --> 01:56:19,900
No!

952
01:56:21,120 --> 01:56:23,020
No!

953
01:56:23,600 --> 01:56:28,180
This is not just a war!

954
01:56:28,230 --> 01:56:34,210
These lives will not be wasted!

955
01:56:34,460 --> 01:56:38,990
This fight is the fight between
good and evil!

956
01:56:40,600 --> 01:56:44,850
We are not going to stop until we
demolish the evil!

957
01:56:44,850 --> 01:56:46,900
We won't, my Osman!

958
01:56:46,900 --> 01:56:49,720
- Of course we won't!
- We will not give up!

959
01:56:49,760 --> 01:56:51,330
We will stand!

960
01:56:51,360 --> 01:56:59,280
We put on our weapons until the true
religion of Allah dominates!

961
01:56:59,730 --> 01:57:04,030
This fight is the fight between
cross and crescent!

962
01:57:05,370 --> 01:57:14,830
- Allah-u Akbar! (Allah is the greatest)
- Allah-u Akbar! (Allah is the greatest)

963
01:57:14,850 --> 01:57:19,130
- Allah-u Akbar! (Allah is the greatest)

964
01:57:19,440 --> 01:57:28,950
- Allah-u Akbar! (Allah is the greatest)

965
01:57:39,400 --> 01:57:41,750
Welcome, Selcan Hatun.

966
01:57:42,640 --> 01:57:48,290
Thank you. I want to see Sheik Edebalı.
I have something to tell him.

967
01:57:48,510 --> 01:57:54,690
Our master is praying for our martyrs
right now. Can you wait?

968
01:59:00,500 --> 01:59:04,150
Finally your face smiles, Osman Bey.

969
01:59:04,660 --> 01:59:07,460
What makes you so?

970
01:59:07,470 --> 01:59:10,280
Tell me so that I can smile too.

971
01:59:12,400 --> 01:59:15,310
I am waiting for my Aunt Selcan, Aygül.

972
01:59:15,310 --> 01:59:19,500
She went to ask for Bala Hatun
in marriage.

973
01:59:23,130 --> 01:59:25,280
Really?

974
01:59:29,000 --> 01:59:32,330
May Allah make you happy.

975
01:59:33,880 --> 01:59:37,070
- May it go well.
- Amin.

976
01:59:38,440 --> 01:59:43,610
Bala Hatun and his father don't cause
trouble, in sha Allah.

977
01:59:44,540 --> 01:59:51,110
But, you know that since they have come to
our tent, we have had a lot of troubles.

978
01:59:52,690 --> 01:59:55,120
Don't talk like that, Aygül.

979
01:59:55,850 --> 01:59:59,830
Trouble comes from Kulucahisar.

980
02:00:00,110 --> 02:00:04,680
May Allah keep Edebalı among us.

981
02:00:05,960 --> 02:00:07,920
As to Bala...

982
02:00:08,950 --> 02:00:11,530
Don't speak of her like this.

983
02:00:12,160 --> 02:00:14,540
I don't want to hurt your feelings.

984
02:00:16,370 --> 02:00:20,070
Okay, Osman Bey.
Okay.

985
02:00:24,690 --> 02:00:28,330
Won't you wish happiness for me?

986
02:00:29,290 --> 02:00:34,340
I'll marry Alişar Bey soon.

987
02:00:39,540 --> 02:00:41,400
Aygül...

988
02:00:42,940 --> 02:00:46,270
You are our pearl in this tribe.

989
02:00:46,910 --> 02:00:51,940
I see you as a sister.

990
02:00:54,410 --> 02:00:59,760
May Allah give you the happiest home.

991
02:01:00,250 --> 02:01:04,430
May you be always happy.

992
02:02:04,320 --> 02:02:07,160
Welcome, Selcan Hatun.

993
02:02:07,230 --> 02:02:09,280
Thank you, my beautiful daughter.

994
02:02:09,480 --> 02:02:13,320
I am happy to see you.

995
02:02:13,340 --> 02:02:16,710
- Thank Allah, we are fine now.
- Thank Allah.

996
02:02:16,820 --> 02:02:19,900
We will see better days, in sha Allah.

997
02:02:19,900 --> 02:02:24,130
I am here to see Sheikh Edebalı for a
good purpose.

998
02:02:26,880 --> 02:02:28,940
Here, Selcan Hatun.

999
02:02:35,510 --> 02:02:41,250
Congratulations, Bala.
May you marry soon.

1000
02:02:42,770 --> 02:02:44,750
Allah gives the best.

1001
02:03:02,310 --> 02:03:04,120
Aygül.

1002
02:03:04,120 --> 02:03:06,810
What happened?

1003
02:03:07,200 --> 02:03:09,300
Nothing, mother.

1004
02:03:12,290 --> 02:03:15,790
Then why are you crying?

1005
02:03:15,840 --> 02:03:18,090
Tell me.

1006
02:03:26,290 --> 02:03:31,340
Mother, I know, you're going to go mad.
But I can't stop it, tolerate me.

1007
02:03:33,010 --> 02:03:35,010
Osman.

1008
02:03:36,960 --> 02:03:40,750
What did he do?
Why did he make you sad?

1009
02:03:40,840 --> 02:03:45,760
He didn't do anything to me, mother.
Selcan Hatun.

1010
02:03:47,680 --> 02:03:51,000
Selcan Hatun has gone to see Edebalı.

1011
02:03:54,210 --> 02:03:57,970
What is she doing there by herself?

1012
02:03:57,970 --> 02:04:01,690
Also, what does she have to talk to with
Edebalı?

1013
02:04:03,120 --> 02:04:05,490
Bala Hatun.

1014
02:04:06,590 --> 02:04:09,990
She will ask for Bala Hatun in marriage
to Osman.

1015
02:04:14,710 --> 02:04:16,880
Look at that.

1016
02:04:17,490 --> 02:04:22,070
Is it her place to act while Osman's
uncle is here?

1017
02:04:22,350 --> 02:04:26,790
They lost it.
Dash away your tear.

1018
02:04:26,820 --> 02:04:30,380
It is because of your vain hopes
about him.

1019
02:04:35,990 --> 02:04:39,690
Your future is bright, my daughter.

1020
02:04:40,030 --> 02:04:44,980
You are going to be a wife of a banner
lord and a Hatun of your tent.

1021
02:04:45,560 --> 02:04:52,710
If Osman goes like this, he will do
nothing but causing trouble.

1022
02:04:53,910 --> 02:04:59,820
Be grateful instead of crying like
a child.

1023
02:05:04,530 --> 02:05:09,490
We have got over a challenging situation,
Selcan Hatun.

1024
02:05:09,670 --> 02:05:11,210
Thank Allah.

1025
02:05:11,810 --> 02:05:17,120
May my Lord make us happy from now on.

1026
02:05:17,370 --> 02:05:19,030
Amin.

1027
02:05:21,810 --> 02:05:27,060
The one to thank is Allah, of course.
However, you did a lot, too.

1028
02:05:27,430 --> 02:05:33,250
You protected my Osman.
May Allah bless you.

1029
02:05:34,790 --> 02:05:38,810
A valiant never walks alone, Selcan Hatun.

1030
02:05:38,910 --> 02:05:46,820
Even if there is no one with him,
if he is with Allah, he is not alone.

1031
02:05:48,090 --> 02:05:50,060
We did nothing.

1032
02:05:50,870 --> 02:05:53,720
Everything happens thanks to our Lord.

1033
02:05:53,720 --> 02:06:03,620
My son Osman challenged with his faith
and got out alive thanks to his faith.

1034
02:06:09,070 --> 02:06:14,330
Sir, you are calling Osman "son".

1035
02:06:14,760 --> 02:06:18,730
We want to call Bala Hatun "daughter".

1036
02:06:19,290 --> 02:06:24,950
Bala Hatun is a very well educated girl.

1037
02:06:26,750 --> 02:06:32,660
If you allow, we want her to brighten our
tribe up.

1038
02:06:34,600 --> 02:06:38,680
With Allah's order and
our Prophet's word...

1039
02:06:38,770 --> 02:06:43,330
We ask for your daughter Bala's hand for
our son Osman.

1040
02:06:55,310 --> 02:06:57,720
Thank you, Hatun.

1041
02:06:58,430 --> 02:07:01,440
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
[in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.]

1042
02:07:17,250 --> 02:07:21,160
I want to tell you something, father.
Do you allow?

1043
02:07:21,700 --> 02:07:26,240
Come here, my daughter.
Here, come.

1044
02:07:34,100 --> 02:07:36,940
I thought it over, father.

1045
02:07:38,770 --> 02:07:43,750
If you allow, I give my consent to
the marriage with Alişar Bey.

1046
02:07:55,130 --> 02:07:57,680
Is this what you want, my daughter?

1047
02:07:58,350 --> 02:08:02,290
Do I or your mother affect your decision?

1048
02:08:02,430 --> 02:08:07,190
No for sure, father.
My tent comes first.

1049
02:08:07,460 --> 02:08:12,590
I know that our tent's fate depends on
this marriage.

1050
02:08:12,820 --> 02:08:18,350
So...
What about your future?

1051
02:08:26,660 --> 02:08:31,100
I just want to see you happy, father.

1052
02:08:31,530 --> 02:08:34,950
May Allah give you the best, my daughter.

1053
02:08:35,810 --> 02:08:42,120
May this marriage bring happiness to you,
power to our tent, in sha Allah.

1054
02:08:45,570 --> 02:08:47,750
In sha Allah.

1055
02:08:48,930 --> 02:08:54,520
In our tradition, Hatuns found home,
and husbands protect it.

1056
02:08:54,980 --> 02:08:59,320
If you wish a happy marriage, know this...

1057
02:08:59,680 --> 02:09:04,620
Flue with smoke, wife with husband.

1058
02:10:23,810 --> 02:10:27,470
You ignited me with love.

1059
02:10:28,700 --> 02:10:33,170
Now, without you...

1060
02:10:33,890 --> 02:10:36,430
there is only death for me, Bala Hatun.

1061
02:10:46,930 --> 02:10:51,260
Our Holy Lord ordered marriage for us.

1062
02:10:51,530 --> 02:10:54,360
Marriage is sacred.

1063
02:10:54,420 --> 02:10:59,060
And marriage is a good purpose, for sure.

1064
02:10:59,580 --> 02:11:05,080
Osman Bey is a strong and fearless man.

1065
02:11:05,190 --> 02:11:11,440
I know that he is a valiant and a strong
warrior.

1066
02:11:14,340 --> 02:11:17,020
As to Bala...

1067
02:11:17,550 --> 02:11:23,700
Bala has been educated with Allah's rules.

1068
02:11:24,560 --> 02:11:27,980
Of course I want her to marry someday.

1069
02:11:31,230 --> 02:11:36,050
However, marriage requires equality.

1070
02:11:37,410 --> 02:11:42,150
If there is no equality, there will be
problems.

1071
02:11:46,130 --> 02:11:49,250
What I am saying is...

1072
02:11:49,850 --> 02:11:54,310
Osman and Bala are not equal.

1073
02:12:00,510 --> 02:12:02,740
I don't want to hurt your feelings.

1074
02:12:03,430 --> 02:12:08,390
But, I don't consent to this marriage.

1075
02:12:32,740 --> 02:12:36,330
My Osman, why are you not eating?

1076
02:12:36,330 --> 02:12:39,580
Your meal is still there.

1077
02:12:39,730 --> 02:12:45,470
Your heart beats so loud that I can hear
it from here.

1078
02:12:49,090 --> 02:12:53,800
Eeh, Bamsı Bey, love issues make you
stop eating.

1079
02:12:53,840 --> 02:12:58,750
Once the wedding ceremony is ready,
I will show everyone how to use a sword!

1080
02:13:00,950 --> 02:13:06,010
Oi, Oi my sharp weapon Osman.

1081
02:13:06,200 --> 02:13:11,700
You are old enough to marry, huh?
Masha Allah (praise be).

1082
02:13:12,140 --> 02:13:15,590
Once this marriage happens...

1083
02:13:15,590 --> 02:13:21,010
I will slaughter forty rams and give this
tribe a feast of food.

1084
02:13:24,300 --> 02:13:29,880
Sergeant Samsa, you should marry too.

1085
02:13:33,480 --> 02:13:37,410
He is famous with his weapons,
Konur brother.

1086
02:13:38,260 --> 02:13:42,210
Mind your own business, Alps.

1087
02:13:42,210 --> 02:13:44,710
Get off my back.

1088
02:13:45,790 --> 02:13:51,260
Erkut Alp, you are very quiet.
What is it?

1089
02:13:51,370 --> 02:13:55,620
Let him be, Abdurrahman Ghazi.
He just wants all of us to marry...

1090
02:13:55,620 --> 02:13:58,280
so that he can eat meat every day.

1091
02:14:05,260 --> 02:14:07,070
Aunt.

1092
02:14:37,120 --> 02:14:39,550
What happened, aunt?

1093
02:14:42,270 --> 02:14:44,480
Why are you upset?

1094
02:14:45,230 --> 02:14:47,260
My Osman.

1095
02:14:49,110 --> 02:14:51,560
Sheikh Edebalı...

1096
02:14:54,370 --> 02:14:57,130
didn't approve.

1097
02:15:06,150 --> 02:15:08,520
He didn't give his consent.

1098
02:15:08,520 --> 02:15:51,530
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com